# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# CSV cache — re-downloaded when you run ingest
.cache/

# Feed snapshots — the one thing under .cache/ that is NOT re-downloadable. The
# open-notice feed is a snapshot of what was open the day it was read, and
# CanadaBuys publishes no history, so a day not copied here is a day gone. Still
# not committed: a year of daily snapshots is hundreds of megabytes, and they
# are local evidence rather than shared source. Redundant under `.cache/` above
# and written out anyway, so that a future narrowing of that line does not
# start committing them by accident.
.cache/snapshots/

# ChromaDB — rebuilt by scripts/ingest/. Not committed, to keep the repo small.
# Anyone cloning runs `python scripts/ingest` once.
chroma_db/

# Sampling runs (--source, --max-audits) write here instead of over the
# real databases; half-finished builds land in .part / .old.
*.sample.db
*.db.part
chroma_db.sample/
chroma_db.old/

# Derived and profile-specific. These are filtered and scored against
# vault/profiles/my-company.md, so they are NOT portable — a different
# profile has to rebuild them, and re-running the ingest is a re-scoring
# rather than a refresh.
#
# data/crosswalk.db is deliberately NOT ignored: it derives from
# org_aliases.yaml, which is a fact about the Government of Canada rather
# than about any one firm, and it's 53KB.
data/contracts.db
data/plans.db
data/oag.db
# Not profile-scored — the lobbying registry is the same for everyone — but
# ignored anyway on size: a three-year window is ~38MB, and the source cannot
# be re-fetched by CI (Cloudflare challenge), so a committed copy would rot
# with nothing able to refresh it. Rebuild locally from the downloaded zip.
data/lobbying.db
data/registrations.db
# Quarantined builds: a database built from a development or archived copy
# rather than an official download, renamed so nothing serves it as current.
data/*UNOFFICIAL
# Hand-acquired source archives. data/source/ is the documented drop path for
# input artifacts that the ingests cannot fetch themselves — currently the OCL
# lobbying zip, which lobbycanada.gc.ca serves only to browsers. Ignored because
# it is bulk upstream data, not something this repo should redistribute.
data/source/
vault/intel/agencies/

# data/notices.db is ignored for a DIFFERENT reason, and the difference is
# worth keeping straight. It is not profile-filtered — notices_ingest stores
# every federal notice with the publisher's own classification, so it would be
# portable. It's 120MB, which is the whole reason: five fiscal years of tender
# and award archives at ~45MB of CSV each. Rebuild it with
# `python scripts/notices_ingest.py`; the archives are static for closed fiscal
# years, so a rebuild returns the same rows rather than a re-scoring.
data/notices.db

# The evidence experiment's derived data. contracts_full.db is the SAME source
# as contracts.db with the profile's IT term filter turned off — 962k rows and
# 383MB, because a capability set spanning the corpus cannot be evidenced from
# a corpus filtered to one firm's categories. casebook.db is its disclosure-date
# derivation. Both rebuild from .cache/contracts.csv:
#   python scripts/contracts_ingest.py --no-term-filter --db data/contracts_full.db \
#          --window-years 12 --no-intel
#   python scripts/casebook.py build-db
data/contracts_full.db
data/casebook.db

# The cases themselves are ignored for a reason that is not size. truth.json
# holds the sealed labels and predictions.jsonl holds what the evaluator said;
# committing them would put the answer key in the repository, and the whole
# protocol depends on the order in which those two files come into existence.
# vault/reference/capabilities.yaml IS committed — the frozen registry is the
# part that has to be public for the run to be reproducible.
data/cases/

# Working state — private. The reference material in vault/reference/ is
# committed because it's how the system works. What we're actually bidding
# on is not.
vault/tenders/
vault/briefings/
vault/searches/
# Department nodes. Same category as vault/tenders/: the directory listing
# alone publishes which departments are being pursued, and the node exists so
# private notes accumulate in it. Durability is Obsidian sync's job, not a
# public repo's.
vault/agencies/

# Obsidian per-machine settings — pane layout, theme, window position
vault/.obsidian/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# The filter audit's replay records. Regenerable by construction: a run is keyed
# on a content-addressed id over the filter version, the corpus fingerprint and
# the as_of spec, so `replay-filter --persist` recreates any run byte for byte.
# Deleting this file loses nothing that is not reproducible.
#
# The audit's EVIDENCE is committed instead, and deliberately elsewhere:
# vault/reference/filter-reviews.jsonl, filter-golden-set.yaml,
# filter-failure-taxonomy.yaml, filter-versions.yaml and filter-refinements/.
# Those are human judgement and belong in a diff; this is scaffolding.
data/filter_audit.db
